  "id": "runtime-limits-expansion-default",
  "description": "Plan v7 section 8.3: the cumulative generated-expansion budget at its DEFAULT of 1,048,576 (1_024 * 1_024), pinned from both sides with no override. Each key is a six-link constant passthrough chain a1..a6 feeding an eighteen-level doubling chain b1..b18 whose leaf is one character, plus a sibling z. Billing is one consume per distinct placeholder: the b chain costs 1+2+...+131072 = 262,143, each of the six a levels costs 131,072 for 786,432, and z costs its own length. z = \"A\" totals exactly 1,048,576 and z = \"AB\" totals 1,048,577. The deepest recursion is 24, inside the default generated-placeholder depth of 32; the largest single expansion is 131,072 and the top-level output is 131,073, both far below the 262,144 interpolated-output default, so the cumulative budget — not the depth cap or the per-output cap — is what decides these two keys.",
